# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
*.egg-info/

# Subagent-driven-development scratch (ledger, task briefs/reports, review packages).
# Local-only working state; may contain absolute paths, so never track it.
.superpowers/

# Local config overlays hold secrets and personal data. Never commit these.
# (sluice.yaml.example is the tracked template; a real sluice.yaml / *.local.yaml
# holds your personal searches, contact details, and hosts.)
*.local.yaml
sluice.local.yaml
/sluice.yaml
*.token
google_token*.json
.env
.env.*

# Runtime artifacts (CV render/serve/apply outputs, dossiers, dedup db,
# health/disabled tracking files)
cv-out/
cv-output/
cv-served/
cv-home/
dossiers/
*.pdf
*_health.json
*_disabled.json
*.db

# AI-tool configs are GENERATED from .rulesync/ via `rulesync generate`. The source of
# truth is .rulesync/ and it IS tracked; everything below is a build artifact. Run
#   npx rulesync@9.6.3 generate -t '*' -f '*'
# after cloning to populate them locally.
#
# Every pattern is ROOT-ANCHORED, and the leading slash is load-bearing: a bare
# `CLAUDE.md` matches at ANY depth and silently swallows the canonical source at
# .rulesync/rules/CLAUDE.md, leaving git with no rules file to clone.
/CLAUDE.md
/AGENTS.md
/GEMINI.md
/.claude/
/.mcp.json
/.cursor/
/.cursorrules
/.github/copilot-instructions.md

# Belt and braces: re-include the canonical source unconditionally. The `/**` is required --
# a bare `!/.rulesync/` re-includes only the DIRECTORY and cannot rescue a file inside it.
!/.rulesync/**

# MemSearch runtime artefacts: session transcripts carrying absolute home paths, session
# UUIDs and PIDs. Never in a public repo.
#
# Deliberately NOT root-anchored, unlike everything above. The anchoring above exists to
# stop a bare `CLAUDE.md` swallowing the canonical source at .rulesync/rules/CLAUDE.md --
# a collision that cannot happen here, since nothing legitimate is named .memsearch/. For
# a directory that has already leaked personal data into this repo twice, catching it at
# ANY depth is the safer default, and there is nothing for it to shadow.
.memsearch/
